<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Têt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Têt is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, about 115 km long, rising in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> near the Carlit massif and flowing past Prades and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perpignan">Perpignan</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. Its fertile, irrigated plain was the economic heart of the medieval county of Roussillon.</p></div>
